{title: 237 - In the Cross of Christ I Glory}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Jesus Christ}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Bb]In the cross of [F7]Christ I glory,
[Bb/D]towering o'er [F]the [Bb]wrecks [C7]of [F]time;
[Bb]all the light [F7]of sacred story
[Bb/D]gathers round its head [F7]sublime.

Verse 2:
[Bb]When the woes of [F7]life o'ertake [Bb]me,
[Bb/D]hopes [Eb]deceive, [F]and [Bb]fears [C7]annoy,
[Bb]never shall [F7]the cross forsake [Bb]me.
[Bb/D]Lo! [Eb]it [Bb]glows with peace [F7]and [Bb]joy.

Verse 3:
[Bb]When the sun of [F7]bliss is beaming
[Bb/D]light [Eb]and [Bb/F]love [F]upon [C7]my [F]way,
[Bb]from the cross [F7]the radiance streaming
[Bb/D]adds [Eb]more [Bb]luster to [F7]the [Bb]day.

Verse 4:
[Bb]Bane and blessing, [F7]pain and pleasure,
[Bb/D]by [Eb]the [Bb/F]cross [F]are [Bb]sanctified;
[Bb]peace is there [F7]that knows no measure,
[Bb/D]joys [Eb]that [Bb]through all time [F7]abide.
